[1m[38;5;231mWhich structural approach should the design use?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: Namespaced global (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246midentity.js defines one AppIdentity global, loaded via script tag before app.js. Matches the existing pattern, page
[39m     [38;5;246mstill opens from disk.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: ES modules
     [38;5;246mConvert to type="module" with real imports/exports. Better encapsulation, but index.html then requires a local [39m
     [38;5;246mserver and app.js execution timing changes.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: Pluggable store + events
     [38;5;246mInjected storage adapter and CustomEvent consent broadcasts. Most flexible and testable, but builds for [39m
     [38;5;246mrequirements that do not exist yet.[39m
